    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.26) anchors the lineup as our most efficient start. Despite a slight park penalty, his matchup against Nick Martinez is gilded by an SP xERA nearing 5.00, and his elite SB potential provides the high-ceiling utility we prioritize. We are also leaning heavily into favorable matchups against RHP Johnson; **Luis Arraez** (69.53), **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.85), and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) are all strong plays here, benefiting from a high-run-environment forecast and a tailwind that adds nearly 5% to their efficiency scores. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** (69.75) finds himself in an excellent spot against Paredes; despite batting ninth, his massive SP skill advantage (xERA 5.35) and platoon edge make him a standout value.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Bryce Harper** (55.05). While his pedigree is unquestionable, the matchup against Weathers\u2014a lefty suppressing his platoon efficiency\u2014and a sub-par SP skill matchup drove his score below our threshold for starting. He came closest to cracking the lineup, but we opted for the higher projected efficiency of **Kyle Karros** (57.22) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (58.90), both of whom benefit from more favorable handedness matchups today. **Cal Raleigh** (46.33) and **Yainer Diaz** (45.97) remain in the lineup as marginal starts; while their base projections are solid, they are battling tough individual SP matchups against Eovaldi and Burke, respectively. We are proceeding without any severe weather alerts, though managers should monitor the status of **Jonathan Aranda** (64.35) as he looks to capitalize on a soft Bibee matchup in a potential high-leverage scoring role.",
